## 7. Testing

**Unit-test the builder** (pure, fast, this is where bugs hide):

```java
class KeysetQueryBuilderTest {
    private final KeysetQueryBuilder b = new KeysetQueryBuilder(OrderTable.DEF, new ValueCoercer());

    @Test
    void appendsTieBreakerAndKeysetPredicate() {
        var req = new QueryRequest(
                List.of(Filter.gte("orderTime", "2025-01-01T00:00:00"), Filter.lt("orderTime", "2025-01-02T00:00:00")),
                List.of(SortOrder.desc("amount")), 50, null);
        var q = b.build(req, List.of("orderId", "amount"), Map.of("amount", "10.00", "orderId", 7));
        assertThat(q.sql()).contains("ORDER BY amount DESC, order_id DESC LIMIT 51")
                           .contains("(amount < :k0) OR (amount = :k0 AND order_id < :k1)");
    }

    @Test
    void rejectsUnboundedTimeRange() {
        var req = new QueryRequest(List.of(Filter.gte("orderTime", "2025-01-01T00:00:00")), List.of(), 50, null);
        assertThrows(QueryValidationException.class, () -> b.build(req, List.of("orderId"), null));
    }
}
